(4545990, 648734, 45475, '<td valign="top">I gave this a 7 purely for composition. A marvellous subject for this challenge. However, I would have given this a 10, without batting an eyelid, had it been in focus somewhere along that road...</td>', 'I gave this a 7 purely for composition. A marvellous subject for this challenge. However, I would have given this a 10, without batting an eyelid, had it been in focus somewhere along that road...', '2008-03-07 15:21:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(4546051, 648696, 45475, '<td valign="top">A little more crop from the top and right hand side would have seen this a more symmetrical and pleasing image. Keep working on that focus.</td>', 'A little more crop from the top and right hand side would have seen this a more symmetrical and pleasing image. Keep working on that focus.', '2008-03-07 15:37:59.000000', NULL, 0),
(4554188, 648757, 90394, '<td valign="top">Nice depiction of a lazy subway station. Fits the theme very well, but way too dark, unless you were going for silouhettes? Alas, I can''t apply that to my score If you were, because this is just too dark, and too bright in the background to the point that my eyes hurt looking at it! lol. More balancing would have made this a fine black and white photo. I''d give this a 5.</td>', 'Nice depiction of a lazy subway station. Fits the theme very well, but way too dark, unless you were going for silouhettes? Alas, I can''t apply that to my score If you were, because this is just too dark, and too bright in the background to the point that my eyes hurt looking at it! lol. More balancing would have made this a fine black and white photo. I''d give this a 5.', '2008-03-11 03:13:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(4562786, 647760, 41337, '<td valign="top">This is expertly focused. Had you focused on the couple it would have ruined the intimacy. The area you did focus on gives it a slight miniature effect that tends to happen when you have a strong background and foreground blur. That in turn gives the image a whole other dynamic. The couple looks even smaller set against the trees (that look more like tall weeds). It''s as if they reached the vanishing point yet the point remains small.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2008-03-13 22:08:29.</i></td>', 'This is expertly focused. Had you focused on the couple it would have ruined the intimacy. The area you did focus on gives it a slight miniature effect that tends to happen when you have a strong background and foreground blur. That in turn gives the image a whole other dynamic. The couple looks even smaller set against the trees (that look more like tall weeds). It''s as if they reached the vanishing point yet the point remains small.', '2008-03-13 22:06:37.000000', '2008-03-13 22:08:29.000000', 0),
(4576765, 648522, 63267, '<td valign="top">This is a wonderful photo.  I can''t see anything in it that I don''t like.  Well captured.</td>', 'This is a wonderful photo.  I can''t see anything in it that I don''t like.  Well captured.', '2008-03-20 12:48:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(4580242, 648604, 44579, '<td valign="top">This is something I would expect to see in a magazine. Then I looked at the score... wow do DPC voters need a lesson in how to break photography rules. This is an amazing image. The framing is unique and artistic, the light is balanced well imo (screw all of you who immediately think an overexposed image is poor), the pose contains sweetness with just enough attitude to make it interesting. I can see what you mean about the eye though, I hate basic editing.<br/> <br/>You are definitely someone who''s photo''s I look to for inspiration. Keep up the good work!</td>', 'This is something I would expect to see in a magazine. Then I looked at the score... wow do DPC voters need a lesson in how to break photography rules. This is an amazing image. The framing is unique and artistic, the light is balanced well imo (screw all of you who immediately think an overexposed image is poor), the pose contains sweetness with just enough attitude to make it interesting. I can see what you mean about the eye though, I hate basic editing. You are definitely someone who''s photo''s I look to for inspiration. Keep up the good work!', '2008-03-22 15:25:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(4591945, 648849, 51538, '<td valign="top">Your photo brings back some pretty good memories; the low light, the spinning disc, the atmosphere.  You captured it all, IMO, and in a nice crisp way.  I''ve been recording some of my vinyl LPs recently and made sure to record those little sounds of the disc as it starts and ends - with even a few scratches on them.  Somehow that sound has more character than digital CDs....  Nice work.</td>', 'Your photo brings back some pretty good memories; the low light, the spinning disc, the atmosphere.  You captured it all, IMO, and in a nice crisp way.  I''ve been recording some of my vinyl LPs recently and made sure to record those little sounds of the disc as it starts and ends - with even a few scratches on them.  Somehow that sound has more character than digital CDs....  Nice work.', '2008-03-27 17:01:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(4603647, 648936, 61654, '<td valign="top">Just curious... Is this the pier in South Haven, MI?</td>', 'Just curious... Is this the pier in South Haven, MI?', '2008-04-01 20:22:34.000000', NULL, 0),
